## DESCRIPTION
## Solve a 4 by 4 linear system.  Solution is a single point.
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject(Linear algebra)
## DBchapter(Systems of linear equations)
## DBsection(Systems with 4 or more variables)
## Date(September 5, 2008)
## Institution(Fitchburg State University)
## Author(Peter Staab)
## KEYWORDS('linear system', 'solution', '4 by 4')

# updated 2023.10.30

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'parserRadioMultiAnswer.pl',,
    'contextFraction.pl', 'MatrixReduce.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context('Vector')->variables->add(
    w => 'Real',
    t => 'Real',
    s => 'Real'
);
Context()->noreduce('(-x)+y', '(-x)-y');

$zerov = Vector([ 0, 0, 0 ]);
# Find a nice matrix with determinant of 1,2,4 or 5.
do {
    $A = Matrix([ map { [ map { random(-5, 5) } (1 .. 4) ] } (1 .. 4) ]);
} until grep { abs($A->det) == $_ } (1, 2, 4, 5);

$x = Vector(map { random(-5, 5) } (1 .. 4));
$b = $A * $x;

@lines = map {
    Formula($A->element($_, 1) . 'x+'
            . $A->element($_, 2) . 'y+'
            . $A->element($_, 3) . 'z+'
            . $A->element($_, 4)
            . 'w')->reduce
} (1 .. 4);

$rma = RadioMultiAnswer(
    [
        ['There is no solution to the linear system'],
        [ 'There is a solution to the linear system in the form %s', $x ]
    ],
    1
);

BEGIN_PGML

Solve the follow linear system using the Gauss-Jordon method.

[```
\begin{aligned}
[$lines[0]] & = [@ Matrix($b)->element(1) @] \\
[$lines[1]] & = [@ Matrix($b)->element(2) @] \\
[$lines[2]] & = [@ Matrix($b)->element(3) @] \\
[$lines[3]] & = [@ Matrix($b)->element(4) @]
\end{aligned}
```]

[_]{$rma}

If there is a solution, write it in vector form, like <1,2,3,4> or <1+t, 2-t, 3+t,4t> and use t and s for free variables if needed.
END_PGML
Context('Fraction');    # for fraction arithmetic

# augmented matrix to be reduced
$aug = Matrix([
    [
        $A->element(1, 1),
        $A->element(1, 2),
        $A->element(1, 3),
        $A->element(1, 4),
        Matrix($b)->element(1)
    ],
    [
        $A->element(2, 1),
        $A->element(2, 2),
        $A->element(2, 3),
        $A->element(2, 4),
        Matrix($b)->element(2)
    ],
    [
        $A->element(3, 1),
        $A->element(3, 2),
        $A->element(3, 3),
        $A->element(3, 4),
        Matrix($b)->element(3)
    ],
    [
        $A->element(4, 1),
        $A->element(4, 2),
        $A->element(4, 3),
        $A->element(4, 4),
        Matrix($b)->element(4)
    ]
]);

$aug_red = rref($aug);

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION

First, start with the augmented coefficient matrix or
[``` [$aug] ```]

and then perform Gauss-Jordon reduction to get 
[``` [$aug_red] ```]

And since the left 4 by 4 matrix is the identity matrix, then the solution is the 
rightmost column or 
[``` \vec{x} = [$x] ```]
END_PGML_SOLUTION
COMMENT('The solution to this nonhomogeneous system is a single point.');
ENDDOCUMENT();
